# Keep agent tooling out of the source archives GitHub attaches to a release.
# It is for working *on* roost, not for building it, and a 424 KiB memory
# store plus four assistants' config in a tarball named `roost-x.y.z` is
# noise at best and stale advice at worst. Cloning still gets all of it.
.claude/ export-ignore
.codex/ export-ignore
.opencode/ export-ignore
.projectmem/ export-ignore
docs/engagements/ export-ignore
AGENTS.md export-ignore
.gitattributes export-ignore
